WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.842
A few numbers capture the impact.

00:00:03.922 --> 00:00:07.764
Moccasin needs only a linear number of integer
variables in the graph size,

00:00:07.844 --> 00:00:11.686
compared to a quadratic number of Boolean variables
for the prior state of the art.

00:00:11.766 --> 00:00:15.608
This translates into solve times up to an order of
magnitude, roughly ten times,

00:00:15.688 --> 00:00:19.530
faster on large graphs.

00:00:19.610 --> 00:00:23.452
And the solutions it finds are high quality: the
total duration increase from rematerialization

00:00:23.532 --> 00:00:27.374
stays consistently below five percent.

00:00:27.454 --> 00:00:31.296
Crucially,

00:00:31.376 --> 00:00:35.218
Moccasin scales to graphs with up to one thousand
nodes and nearly six thousand edges,

00:00:35.298 --> 00:00:39.140
a regime where the competing method simply times
out or runs out of memory.
